# Agent context index

`.agents/agc-index.md` is the **index of all project instructions**. Read it first in every session, then open only the `agc-*` files it points to.

## Required flow

1. Read `.agents/agc-index.md`.
2. Open the listed file that matches the task:
   - Overview / product: `.agents/agc-overview.md`
   - Libraries, hosting, auth, deploy: `.agents/agc-tech-stack.md`
   - Pages, Cloud Run, Firestore: `.agents/agc-main-services.md`
3. Follow those files. Do not assume a bundler, npm app, or framework.

## Guardrails

```text
❌ BAD: Start coding as if this were React/Next, or invent new order status enums.
✅ GOOD: Read agc-index, then edit the existing HTML page and keep Arabic statuses / Firebase contracts.
```

When you add a lasting convention, update the matching `agc-*` file and add a row in `agc-index.md`.
